  {
    "episode_id": 81271,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81271.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, we love you for your continued power. And like you said, being yourself as a woman, a black woman, as somebody with a disability, all of these things are so often treated as disruptions against the status quo. And I would say that's how the squad has been received by some people, including the former twice impeached president. So you, Alexandria Acasio-Cortez, Ilhan Omar, Cory Bush, Rashida Tlaib, and more, you all have been known as the squad. It keeps expanding and growing beautifully. But like I said, many have tried to co-opt and weaponize this term, the squad. So how do you define the squad?",
